From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernardo Pereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 11:48:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rebuild nested shadow layout children

Incremental propagation visits DOM children omitted from a cached
layout_children list, but retaining that cache still hid newly inserted
nested shadow content. Clear it on CONSTRUCT_BOX damage and mark
inserted parents dirty so the next layout pass collects the new
children.

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: only the mutator half remains.
Upstream's propagate walk always visits the DOM children (no cached
layout_children branch), and every node whose damage carries
CONSTRUCT_BOX, own or bubbled up from a child, re-collects in
resolve_layout_children, so the cache clear in damage.rs is absorbed.
---
 src/mutator.rs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/mutator.rs b/src/mutator.rs
index 5c81a3f..a799d86 100644
--- a/src/mutator.rs
+++ b/src/mutator.rs
@@ -907,6 +907,7 @@ impl DocumentMutator<'_> {
             {
                 data.hint |= RestyleHint::restyle_subtree();
             }
+            new_parent.set_dirty_descendants();
             // Mark ancestors dirty so the style traversal visits this subtree.
             new_parent.mark_ancestors_dirty();
         }
